  "answer": "Citation complaints decreased sharply from Q1 to Q2 after the April 2026 citation validation engine and PDF parser update. Support ticket data for citation accuracy shows a drop from 88 tickets in March to 42 in April, 31 in May, and 24 in June [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. The Q2 report confirms citation-related complaints declined steadily and significantly, with remaining tickets linked almost entirely to scanned, image-only PDFs [NL-011#NL-011-S05][NL-016#NL-016-S04].\n\nThe planned product work that directly addresses the remaining scanned-document problem is the **Advanced OCR Pipeline**. The Q1 action items recommend implementing an integrated OCR pipeline to address scanned PDF challenges, with a target to launch an OCR pilot by August 2026 [NL-010#NL-010-S10]. This is confirmed in later discussions: “We are actively developing an Advanced OCR Pipeline, which is scheduled for release in August 2026,” which will extract text and layout from scanned files to enable page-specific citations [NL-024#NL-024-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
